# maid

Running script:

1. Install "Blender Development" VS Code extension.
2. Run "Blender: Start" command in VS Code. This launches a special Blender instance.
3. Open a Blender project.
4. Model and animate. One note: I get color by `material.node_tree.nodes["Principled BSDF"].inputs["Base Color"].default_value`.
5. Run "Blender: Run Script" command in VS Code. Alternatively, set up a hotkey (I use Ctrl+Shift+Enter) to run this.
6. Files will write to `constants.STORYBOARD_FOLDER`, including image and storyboard files.